 ('TXT_KEY_PALEO_CIV5_HEADING_1','The Ancient Earth'),
 ('TXT_KEY_PALEO_CIV5_TEXT_1','The Paleontological Directorate is an eccentric scientific republic devoted to the ancient earth. Its scholars unearth fossils and preserve antiquities, gathering evidence of lost ecosystems in grand museums. Patience and curiosity guide its universities, while field expeditions carry discovery beyond its borders.'),
 ('TXT_KEY_PALEO_CIV5_HEADING_2','The Earth Remembers'),
 ('TXT_KEY_PALEO_CIV5_TEXT_2','Each city with a Library-class building gains +1 [ICON_RESEARCH] Science. Independently, each city with a University-class building gains +1 [ICON_CULTURE] Culture. Real or free buildings and unique replacements qualify; each class grants its bonus once per city.'),
 ('TXT_KEY_PALEO_CIV5_FACTOID_HEADING','A Republic of Discovery'),
 ('TXT_KEY_PALEO_CIV5_FACTOID_TEXT','The earth remembers more than any archive.'),
 ('TXT_KEY_PALEO_OTHMAR_NAME','Director Emeritus Othmar'),
 ('TXT_KEY_PALEO_OTHMAR_SUBTITLE','Keeper of the Ancient Earth'),
 ('TXT_KEY_PALEO_OTHMAR_LIVED','Fictional scientific republic'),
 ('TXT_KEY_PALEO_OTHMAR_TITLES_1','Director Emeritus'),
 ('TXT_KEY_PALEO_OTHMAR_HEADING_1','The Collections Must Endure'),
 ('TXT_KEY_PALEO_OTHMAR_TEXT_1','Director Emeritus Othmar, Keeper of the Ancient Earth, is a stout elderly fossil scholar with an enormous magnifying monocle, wild white side-whiskers, an ivory laboratory coat and a vermilion waistcoat. He cradles prized ammonites as though they were beloved pets. He welcomes visitors to a gigantic museum whose most imposing dinosaur skeleton is not quite correctly assembled. Generally peaceful, he is fiercely protective of scientific access and the collections.'),
 ('TXT_KEY_PALEO_OTHMAR_FACT_1','Othmar keeps fossils in every pocket of his field coat.');
